  "name": "Question 16",
  "problem": "The rate, in degrees Farhenheit per month, at which the average midday temperature in New York City varies, does so according to the function $R(t)={t}^{3}+3,$ where $t$ is the number of months since the measurements began. Estimate the total increase in air temperature over the first three months using the trapezoidal rule with $3$ trapezoids of equal height.",
  "worked_solution": "In this context, the area $A$ under the curve $y=R(t)$ over the interval $[0,3]$ represents the total increase in air temperature over the first three months.\n\nThe general formula for the trapezoidal rule states that\n\n$$\nA\u2248\\frac{1}{2}[R(a)+2(R({t}_{1})+R({t}_{2})+\u22ef+R({t}_{n-1}))+R(b)]\u0394t,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of trapezoids and $\u0394t=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ is the step size.\n\nHere, we have the following values:\n\n- The number of trapezoids is $n=3.$\n\n- The corresponding interval is $[0,3],$ so we have $a=0$ and $b=3.$\n\n- The step size is given by\n\n$$\n\u0394t=\\frac{b-a}{n}=\\frac{3-0}{3}=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above values, the general formula becomes\n\n$$\nA\u2248\\frac{1}{2}[R(0)+2(R(1)+R(2))+R(3)]\\cdot 1.\n$$\n\nTo identify the function values, we now set up a table with the values of $t$ and $R(t):$\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $R(t)$ | $3$ | $4$ | $11$ | $30$ |\n\nSubstituting the appropriate numbers into the above expression gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & \u2248\\frac{1}{2}[3+2(4+11)+30]\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{63}{2} \\\\  & =31.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total air temperature increase is approximately ${31.5}^{\u2218}\\,\\text{F}.$",
